     "content": "Required practical activity 1 (listed under 4.1.1.2 Animal and plant cells): use a light microscope to observe, draw and label a selection of plant and animal cells. A magnification scale must be included. Apparatus and techniques covered: AT 1 – use appropriate apparatus to record length and area; AT 7 – use a microscope to make observations of biological specimens and produce labelled scientific drawings. Key opportunities for skills development: MS 1d, 3a – use estimations to judge the relative size or area of sub-cellular structures."
